From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: bb's cloud plugins are not shipped

1ma does not ship bb's cloud services, which send data to getbb.app, until
1ma runs its own. BB_CLOUD_PLUGIN_NAMES in @bb/domain lists bb-account,
bb-ai, connect and connect-next; the server and the desktop app both read
it.

Server: the plugins stay in BUNDLED_PLUGINS, because bb's catalog generator
needs an entry for each item there, but SHIPPED_PLUGINS and the bundled
registrations leave them out, and the bb-app tarball smoke test no longer
expects bb connect to be running in a fresh install. A data folder that
comes from bb (desktop/scripts/migrate-from-bb.mjs in the 1ma repository)
carries these plugins: bb's orphan cleanup removes their rows; for these
four it also deletes their key-value storage and their plugins/<id> folder,
where sign-ins to bb's cloud live (owner decision, 17.11.2026). A cloud
plugin the user removed earlier keeps a row with removedAt; those rows are
purged the same way.

Desktop: without connect the app starts no account server sync, session
renewal or machine enrollment and opens no sign-in window, so the Server
menu has no "Sign in to bb Connect" item and none of connect's code reaches
getbb.app. The server target store drops a saved connect server on load and
never chooses or adopts one. A server that moved away through bb connect is
not opened: the moved-server page explains it and offers only Choose server.

Desktop, the saved server list: bb reads server-target.json once at start
and treats any read error as "no file", so the next change writes an empty
list over the saved servers. A file that exists but could not be read is now
left alone for that start: changes stay in memory, and a move to a direct
server is not recorded as shown, so the next start repeats it.

The AI services text and search keyword no longer mention bb cloud.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
